## Mojo 0.26.2 CRITICAL Constraints
1. `@extern` and `fn`/`def` must be on SEPARATE lines — no `@extern("X") fn foo():`
2. `for` and `if` must be on OWN lines — no `if x > 0: do_something()` on same line after colon
3. Two statements on one line separated by `;` DO work for non-var statements: `a+=1; b+=2`
4. `var decl; var decl2` separated by `;` does NOT work — each var needs its own line
5. Functions returning `List[Float32]` with complex bodies trigger compiler SEGFAULT during codegen
6. Simple functions returning `List[Float32]` (like list_add, rms_norm) DO compile
7. NO tuple return types `-> (List[Float32], List[Float32])` — not supported
8. NO struct initializer at runtime `MyBuf{ptr: X, size: Y}` — not supported
9. String concat + C bridge (`d + "emb.bin"` passed to C) causes runtime crash
10. Always use LITERAL paths for load_file_data: `_ld("/path/to/file.bin")`

